{
  "title": "Ziyarat of Abd al-Azim al-Hasani",
  "data": "At the tomb of Abd al-Azim al-Hasani, recite:\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى اٰدَمَ صِفْوَةِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA AADAMA SIFWATILLAAH\nPeace be upon Adam the choice of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى نُوْحٍ نَبِيِّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA NOOHIN NABIYYILLAAH\nPeace be upon Noah the prophet of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰىۤ اِبْرَاهِيْمَ خَلِيْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA IBRAAHEEMA KHALEELILLAAH\nPeace be upon Abraham the friend of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى مُوْسٰى كَلِيْمِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA MOOSAA KALEEMILLAAH\nPeace be upon Moses the spoken by Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى عِيْسٰى رُوْحِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA I'EESAA ROOHILLAAH\nPeace be upon Jesus the spirit of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا رَسُوْلَ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA RASOOLALLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O Allah’s Messenger.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا خَيْرَ خَلْقِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA KHAYRA KHALQILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O Allah’s best creature.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا صَفِيَّ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA SAFIYYALLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O elite of Allah.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُحَمَّدَ بْنَ عَبْدِ اللّٰهِ خَاتَمَ النَّبِيِّيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MUHAMMADABNA A'BDILLAAHI KHAATAMAN NABIYYEEN\nPeace be upon you, O Muhammad the son of 'Abdullah and the seal of the Prophets.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَاۤ اَمِيْرَ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ عَلِيَّ بْنَ اَبِيْ طَالِبٍ وَصِيَّ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA AMEERAL MU'MINEENA A'LIYYABNA ABEE TAALIBIN WASIYYA RASOOLILLAAH\nPeace be upon you, O Commander of the Faithful ‘Ali the son of Abu-Talib and the successor of Allah’s Messenger.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ يَا فَاطِمَةُ سَيِّدَةَ نِسَاۤءِ الْعَالَمِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKI YAA FAATIMATU SAYYIDATA NISAA'IL A'ALAMEEN\nPeace be upon you, O Fatimah the doyenne of the women of the worlds.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمَا يَا سِبْطَيِ الرَّحْمَةِ وَسَيِّدَيْ شَبَابِ اَهْلِ الْجَنَّةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKUMAA YAA SIBTAYIR RAHMATI WA SAYYIDAY SHABAABI AHLIL JANNAH\nPeace be upon both of you, O grandsons of the Mercy and two chiefs of the youth of Paradise.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَلِيَّ بْنَ الْحُسَيْنِ سَيِّدَ الْعَابِدِيْنَ وَقُرَّةَ عَيْنِ النَّاظِرِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'LIYYABNAL HUSAYNI SAYYIDAL A'ABIDEENA WA QURRATA A'YNIN NAAZIREEN\nPeace be upon you, O ‘Ali the son of al-Husayn, the chief of the worshippers and the delight of the eye of all seers.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُحَمَّدَ بْنَ عَلِيٍّ بَاقِرَ الْعِلْمِ بَعْدَ النَّبِيِّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MUHAMMADABNA A'LIYYIN BAAQIRAL I'LMI BA'DAN NABIYY\nPeace be upon you, O Muhammad the son of ‘Ali, the splitter of knowledge after the Prophet.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا جَعْفَرَ بْنَ مُحَمَّدٍ الصَّادِقَ الْبَآرَّ الْاَمِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA JA'FARABNA MUHAMMADINIS SAADIQAL BAARRAL AMEEN\nPeace be upon you, O Ja'far the son of Muhammad, the veracious, dutiful, and honest.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُوْسَى بْنَ جَعْفَرٍ الطَّاهِرَ الطُّهْرَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MOOSABNA JA'FARINIT TAAHIRAT TUHR\nPeace be upon you, O Musa the son of Ja'far, the immaculate and ever-pure.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَلِيَّ بْنَ مُوْسَى الرِّضَا الْمُرْتَضٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'LIYYABNA MOOSAR RIDAL MURTADAA\nPeace be upon you, O ‘Ali the son of Musa, the well-pleased and well-contented.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مُحَمَّدَ بْنَ عَلِيٍّ التَّقِيَّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MUHAMMADABNA A'LIYYINIT TAQIYY\nPeace be upon you, O Muhammad the son of ‘Ali, the pious.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا عَلِيَّ بْنَ مُحَمَّدٍ النَّقِيَّ النَّاصِحَ الْاَمِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA A'LIYYABNA MUHAMMADININ NAQIYYAN NAASIHAL AMEEN\nPeace be upon you, O ‘Ali the son of Muhammad, the immaculate, sincere, and honest.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا حَسَنَ بْنَ عَلِيٍّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA HASANABNA A'LIYY\nPeace be upon you, O Hasan the son of ‘Ali.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْوَصِيِّ مِنْ بَعْدِهٖ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL WASIYYI MIN BA'DIH\nPeace be upon the next successor.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ صَلِّ عَلٰى نُوْرِكَ وَسِرَاجِكَ وَوَلِيِّ وَلِيِّكَ\nALLAAHUMMA SALLI A'LAA NOORIKA WA SIRAAJIKA WA WALIYYI WALIYYIK\nO Allah, send blessings upon Your light, Your lantern, the representative of Your representative,\nوَوَصِيِّ وَصِيِّكَ وَحُجَّتِكَ عَلٰى خَلْقِكَ\nWA WASIYYI WASIYYIKA WA HUJJATIKA A'LAA KHALQIK\nthe successor of Your successor, and the argument of You against Your creatures.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ اَيُّهَا السَّيِّدُ الزَّكِيُّ وَالطَّاهِرُ الصَّفِيُّ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA AYYUHAS SAYYIDUZ ZAKIYYU WAT TAAHIRUS SAFIYY\nPeace be upon you, O bright chief and well-selected, immaculate one.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ السَّادَةِ الْاَطْهَارِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNAS SAADATIL AT-HAAR\nPeace be upon you, O son of the immaculate chiefs.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا ابْنَ الْمُصْطَفَيْنَ الْاَخْيَارِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YABNAL MUSTAFAYNAL AKHYAAR\nPeace be upon you, O son of the well-chosen, upright ones.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلٰى رَسُولِ اللّٰهِ وَعَلٰى ذُرِّيَّةِ رَسُوْلِ اللّٰهِ وَرَحْمَةُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكَاتُهٗ.\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAA RASOOLILLAAHI WA A'LAA DHURRIYYATI RASOOLILLAAHI WA RAHMATULLAAHI WA BARAKAATUH\nPeace be upon Allah’s Messenger and upon the progeny of Allah’s Messenger. Allah’s mercy and blessings be upon them.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَى الْعَبْدِ الصَّالِحِ الْمُطِيْعِ لِلّٰهِ رَبِّ الْعَالَمِيْنَ وَلِرَسُوْلِهٖ وَلِاَمِيْرِ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAL A'BDIS SAALIHIL MUTEE'I LILLAAHI RABBIL A'ALAMEENA WA LIRASOOLIHEE WA LI-AMEERIL MU'MINEEN\nPeace be upon the righteous servant, obedient to Allah the Lord of the worlds, to His Messenger, and to the Commander of the Faithful.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا اَبَا الْقَاسِمِ ابْنَ السِّبْطِ الْمُنْتَجَبِ الْمُجْتَبٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA ABAL QAASIMIBNAS SIBTIL MUNTAJABIL MUJTABAA\nPeace be upon you, O Abu’l-Qasim the son of the preferred and well-selected grandson.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ يَا مَنْ بِزِيَارَتِهٖ ثَوَابُ زِيَارَةِ سَيِّدِ الشُّهَدَاۤءِ يُرْتَجٰى\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA YAA MAN BIZIYAARATIHEE THAWAABU ZIYAARATI SAYYIDISH SHUHADAA'I YURTAJAA\nPeace be upon you, O he in the visiting of whose tomb, the reward of visiting the Master of the Martyrs is hoped.\nاَلسَّلَامُ عَلَيْكَ عَرَّفَ اللّٰهُ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكُمْ فِي الْجَنَّةِ\nAS-SALAAMU A'LAYKA A'RRAFALLAAHU BAYNANAA WA BAYNAKUM FIL JANNAH\nPeace be upon you. May Allah introduce us to you all in Paradise,\nوَحَشَرَنَا فِيْ زُمْرَتِكُمْ وَاَوْرَدَنَا حَوْضَ نَبِيِّكُمْ\nWA HASHARANAA FEE ZUMRATIKUM WA AWRADANAA HAWDA NABIYYIKUM\ninclude us with your group, allow us to approach the pond of your Prophet,\nوَسَقَانَا بِكَاْسِ جَدِّكُمْ مِنْ يَدِ عَلِيِّ بْنِ اَبِيْ طَالِبٍ\nWA SAQAANAA BIKA'SI JADDIKUM MIN YADI A'LIYYIBNI ABEE TAALIB\nand serve us with water from the cup of your grandfather and from the hand of ‘Ali the son of Abu-Talib.\nصَلَوَاتُ اللّٰهِ عَلَيْكُمْ\nSALAWAATULLAAHI A'LAYKUM\nAllah’s blessings be upon you all.\nاَسْاَلُ اللّٰهَ اَنْ يُرِيَنَا فِيْكُمُ السُّرُوْرَ وَالْفَرَجَ\nAS'ALULLAAHA AN YURIYANAA FEEKUMUS SUROORA WAL FARAJ\nI beseech Allah to show us delight and relief through you,\nوَاَنْ يَجْمَعَنَا وَاِيَّاكُمْ فِيْ زُمْرَةِ جَدِّكُمْ مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَاٰلِهِ\nWA AN YAJMA'ANAA WA IYYAAKUM FEE ZUMRATI JADDIKUM MUHAMMADIN SALLALLAAHU A'LAYHI WA AALIH\nto join us with you in the group of your grandfather Muhammad, Allah’s blessings be upon him and his Household,\nوَاَنْ لَا يَسْلُبَنَا مَعْرِفَتَكُمْ اِنَّهٗ وَلِيٌّ قَدِيْرٌ\nWA AN LAA YASLUBANAA MA'RIFATAKUM INNAHOO WALIYYUN QADEER\nand never to deprive us of our recognition of you. Verily, He is Guardian and All-powerful.\nاَتَقَرَّبُ اِلَى اللّٰهِ بِحُبِّكُمْ وَالْبَرَاۤءَةِ مِنْ اَعْدَاۤئِكُمْ\nATAQARRABU ILALLAAHI BIHUBBIKUM WAL BARAA'ATI MIN A'DAA'IKUM\nI seek nearness to Allah through my love for you, repudiation of your enemies,\nوَالتَّسْلِيْمِ اِلَى اللّٰهِ رَاضِيًا بِهٖ غَيْرَ مُنْكِرٍ وَلَا مُسْتَكْبِرٍ\nWAT TASLEEMI ILALLAAHI RAADIYAN BIHEE GHAYRA MUNKIRIN WA LAA MUSTAKBIR\nand submission to Allah, accepting Him without denial or arrogance,\nوَعَلٰى يَقِيْنِ مَا اَتٰى بِهٖ مُحَمَّدٌ\nWA A'LAA YAQEENI MAA ATAA BIHEE MUHAMMAD\nbeing fully certain of what Muhammad has brought.\nنَطْلُبُ بِذٰلِكَ وَجْهَكَ يَا سَيِّدِيْ اَللّٰهُمَّ وَرِضَاكَ وَالدَّارَ الْاٰخِرَةَ\nNATLUBU BIDHAALIKA WAJHAKA YAA SAYYIDEE ALLAAHUMMA WA RIDAAKA WAD DAARAL AAKHIRAH\nWe, through this, only seek Your Face, O my Master Allah, and Your satisfaction as well as the Next Abode.\nيَا سَيِّدِيْ وَابْنَ سَيِّدِي اشْفَعْ لِيْ فِي الْجَنَّةِ\nYAA SAYYIDEE WABNA SAYYIDISH FA' LEE FIL JANNAH\nO my master and son of my master, (please) intercede for me to win Paradise,\nفَاِنَّ لَكَ عِنْدَ اللّٰهِ شَاْنًا مِنَ الشَّاْنِ\nFA-INNA LAKA I'NDALLAAHI SHA'NAN MINASH SHA'N\nfor you enjoy an outstanding status with Allah.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اِنِّيۤ اَسْاَلُكَ اَنْ تَخْتِمَ لِيْ بِالسَّعَادَةِ\nALLAAHUMMA INNEE AS'ALUKA AN TAKHTIMA LEE BIS SA'AADAH\nO Allah, I do beseech You to seal my life with happiness;\nفَلَا تَسْلُبْ مِنِّيْ مَا اَنَا فِيْهِ\nFALAA TASLUB MINNEE MAA ANAA FEEH\nso, (please) do not deprive me of that which I enjoy.\nوَلَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ الْعَلِيِّ الْعَظِيْمِ\nWA LAA HAWLA WA LAA QUWWATA ILLAA BILLAAHIL A'LIYYIL A'ZEEM\nThere is neither might nor power except with Allah the All-high and All-great.\nاَللّٰهُمَّ اسْتَجِبْ لَنَا وَتَقَبَّلْهُ بِكَرَمِكَ وَعِزَّتِكَ وَبِرَحْمَتِكَ وَعَافِيَتِكَ\nALLAAHUMMAS TAJIB LANAA WA TAQABBALHU BIKARAMIKA WA I'ZZATIKA WA BIRAHMATIKA WA A'AFIYATIK\nO Allah, (please) respond to us and accept this from us in the name of Your generosity, almightiness, mercy, and bestowal of wellbeing.\nوَصَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلٰى مُحَمَّدٍ وَاٰلِهِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ وَسَلَّمَ تَسْلِيْمًا\nWA SALLALLAAHU A'LAA MUHAMMADIN WA AALIHEE AJMA'EENA WA SALLAMA TASLEEMAA\nMay Allah bless Muhammad and his entire Household and pour down peace on them,\nيَاۤ اَرْحَمَ الرَّاحِمِيْنَ.\nYAA ARHAMAR RAAHIMEEN\nO most merciful of all those who show mercy.",
  "merits": "No ziyarat narrated for Abd al-Azim al-Hasani himself has come down to us. Fakhr al-Muhaqqiqin, Jamal al-Din, states in his book al-Mazar that it is most appropriate to recite this form of ziyarat at his tomb.\n\nIn his book of al-Rawashih, al-Muhaqqiq al-Damad says that the rewards of visiting the tomb of ‘Abd al-’Azim al-Hasani have been mentioned in confirmative traditions. One of these traditions reads that whoever visits his tomb will be awarded Paradise inevitably. This very tradition has been also mentioned by al-Shahid al-Thani in the margin of his book of al-Khulasah as reported from some experts in lineages.\n\nIbn Babawayh and Ibn Qawlawayh have reported through a valid chain of authority that a man from the people of Ray visited Imam ‘Ali al-Hadi (a.s.) who asked him where from he had come. “I came here after I had visited Imam al-Husayn,” answered the man. The Imam (a.s.) said, “Actually, if you had visited the tomb of ‘Abd al-’Azim in your city, you would have been as if you have visited al-Husayn ibn ‘Ali, peace be upon them.”\n\nThe lineage of ‘Abd al-’Azim al-Hasani (known as Shah ‘Abd al-’Azim), the great personality, goes back through four lines to Imam al-Hasan al-Mujtaba the grandson of the best of all creatures; namely, the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him and his Household.\n\n‘Abd al-’Azim is thus the son of ‘Abdullah the son of ‘Ali the son of al-Hasan the son of Zayd the son of al-Hasan the son of ‘Ali the son of Abu-Talib. His holy tomb, which is in the city of Ray (southern Tehran, Iran), is famous. It is a haven and a shelter for the publics. The high standing and majestic position of ‘Abd al-’Azim is clearer than sunlight. First of all, he is from the descendants of the Seal of the Prophets. He is also one of the master traditionists, great scholars, ascetics, and worshippers, and well-known for his distinguished religiousness and piety. He was within the companions of Imam al-Jawad and Imam al-Hadi whom he used to take as means to Almighty Allah and to whom he adhered distinguishably. He also reported many traditions from these two Holy Imams.\n\nHe was the author of the books entitled Khutab Amir al-Mu’minin (Sermons of the Commander of the Faithful) and al-Yawm wal-Laylah (The Day and the Night).\n\nHis story of presenting his beliefs before Imam al-Hadi (a.s.) is famous. The Imam (a.s.) then said to him, “O Abu’l-Qasim, this is by Allah the very religion that Allah has accepted for His servants; therefore, you should keep on it. Allah may strengthen your faith by the true Words in this world and in the life to come.”\n\nAl-Sahib ibn ‘Abbad wrote a brief thesis about the biography of this man. This thesis has been quoted by our mentor Shaykh al-Nuri in the epilogue of his book entitled al-Mustadrak.\n\nIn this book, as well as the famous book of biography known as Rijal al-Kashshi, it has been recorded that when ‘Abd al-’Azim feared for himself the persecution of the ruling authorities, he had to leave for several countries disguising. He then came to the city of Ray and resided in Sarbanan. He confided himself in a vault in a house of a Shi’ite man in a place called Sikkat al-Mawla. He used to worship Almighty Allah in that vault by spending his days fasting and his nights doing acts of worship. Disguising himself, he used to leave that vault for visiting the tomb that would be opposite to his tomb at the other side of the road. He used to say that the tomb was for one of the descendants of Imam Musa ibn Ja’far al-Kazim, peace be upon him. During his stay in that vault, the Shi’ah reported his manners to one another until he was known by the majority of them. One night, one of these Shi’ah saw in dream the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) saying to him, “One of my descendants will be carried from Sikkat al-Mawla and buried next to that apple tree in the orchard of ‘Abd al-Jabbar the son of ‘Abd al-Wahhab. The man therefore went to the owner of that orchard and offered to buy that tree and its place. The owner of the orchard asked, “What for are you asking me to sell you that very tree and its place?” The man had to inform him about his dream. The owner then told him that he had seen a similar dream and, as a result, he endowed that tree and its place to the sayyids and the Shi’ah to bury their dead ones there.\n\nAfter that, ‘Abd al-’Azim became ill and passed away. May Allah have mercy upon him. When he was stripped of his clothes for performing the ritual bathing for his dead body, a sheet of paper was found in his pocket. In that sheet of paper, he had written down his lineage as follows: “I am Abu’l-Qasim ‘Abd al-’Azim the son of ‘Abdullah the son of ‘Ali the son of al-Hasan the son of Zayd the son of al-Hasan the son of ‘Ali the son of Abu-Talib.”\n\nDescribing the knowledgeability of ‘Abd al-’Azim, al-Sahib ibn ‘Abbad says that Abu-Turab al-Rawayani has reported that he heard Abu-Hammad al-Razi saying: One day, I visited Imam ‘Ali al-Naqi (al-Hadi) in Samarra’ and asked him about some legal and illegal issues of the religion. The Imam (a.s.) answered all of my questions. When I bid farewell to him, he said to me, “Hammad, if you face any problem regarding your religious affairs while you are in your hometown (i.e. Ray), you may ask ‘Abd al-’Azim ibn ‘Abdullah al-Hasani. Once you do, convey my greetings to him.”"
}
